      "message": "[warning] Line 2317: 🟡 `isAuthorizedLocalCommit` ends with `return mode() !\u003d ConversationMode::DOCUMENT \u0026\u0026 hasLocalPermission(Permission::Text);`, which authorizes any unhandled/unknown commit type in non-document conversations as long as the sender can post text. That breaks the explicit deny-by-default model and can silently grant permission to newly introduced `CommitType` values if this function is not updated. Replace this fallback with `return false` and handle every allowed commit type explicitly (including any intentional legacy type) so new types fail closed.",
